      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.34,
          "en": "So we got our code opened up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.34,
          "end": 6.83,
          "en": "We created this project with Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.83,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "Now it would be nice to preview our app because of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 12.58,
          "en": "whilst we're working on the React Native app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.58,
          "end": 14.67,
          "en": "we want to constantly preview it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.67,
          "end": 16.47,
          "en": "so that we can see our changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.47,
          "end": 18.94,
          "en": "and tweak the app as required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.94,
          "end": 22.269,
          "en": "It would basically be nice to have the same kind of workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.269,
          "end": 24.63,
          "en": "or a comparable workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.63,
          "end": 28.16,
          "en": "as we have it with the browser and just React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.16,
          "end": 30.31,
          "en": "when we're building React Web apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.31,
          "end": 32.65,
          "en": "There, we can also create a React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.65,
          "end": 34.6,
          "en": "and preview it in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.6,
          "end": 37.25,
          "en": "Now thankfully, since we're using Expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.25,
          "end": 41.973,
          "en": "previewing our app on a real device is super easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.89,
          "end": 46.11,
          "en": "You just need an Android device or an iPhone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 48.57,
          "en": "In my case, I have an iPhone here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.57,
          "end": 50.79,
          "en": "but the same is true for Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 53.38,
          "en": "and you visit the app store there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.38,
          "end": 56.933,
          "en": "And in the app store, you can search for Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.36,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "Now, you should find a Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "This is an app provided by the company behind the Expo CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 69.883,
          "en": "and this Expo package, which is part of our project here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.72,
          "end": 74.42,
          "en": "So you can now download this app onto your device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.42,
          "end": 77.06,
          "en": "This app is available for the iPhone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.06,
          "end": 79.28999999999999,
          "en": "and for Android devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.28999999999999,
          "end": 81.873,
          "en": "And once downloaded, you can open it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.03,
          "end": 87.65,
          "en": "Now in here, you can preview your Expo apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.65,
          "end": 91.35,
          "en": "that are built on your local computer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.35,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "To do that, you should open up your terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 95.18,
          "en": "or command prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.18,
          "end": 98.33,
          "en": "Here, I'm using the one integrated into VS Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.33,
          "end": 100.44,
          "en": "You can open this by going to terminal here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 101.82,
          "en": "and opening a new terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.82,
          "end": 105.19,
          "en": "And this is the default system terminal integrated here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.19,
          "end": 107.35,
          "en": "into your VS Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.35,
          "end": 110.893,
          "en": "And then in here you can run npm-start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 113.33,
          "en": "Now, what this will do, (device chiming)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.33,
          "end": 117.61,
          "en": "is it will actually start the Expo Development Server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.61,
          "end": 119.69,
          "en": "which watches and builds our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.69,
          "end": 121.4,
          "en": "and which builds our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.4,
          "end": 124.06,
          "en": "basically such that we can preview it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.06,
          "end": 127.28,
          "en": "And it also gives us a QR code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.28,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "You can scan this QR code with your Expo app on Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 132.61,
          "en": "not on iOS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.61,
          "end": 133.85,
          "en": "I'll come back to this in a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.85,
          "end": 137.14,
          "en": "but on Android, you will have a barcode scanner,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.14,
          "end": 139.941,
          "en": "a button that allows you to scan this barcode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.941,
          "end": 142.823,
          "en": "in your Expo Go app which you downloaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.88,
          "end": 146.65,
          "en": "In addition, you also should have a browser tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.65,
          "end": 151.03,
          "en": "that opened up where you also find this barcode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.03,
          "end": 154.8,
          "en": "and where you will find log messages printed by Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.8,
          "end": 156.323,
          "en": "as your app is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.5,
          "end": 160.69,
          "en": "Now on the iPhone, the scanner is not integrated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.69,
          "end": 162.64,
          "en": "into the Expo app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.64,
          "end": 164.94,
          "en": "Instead, there you need to open your camera",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.94,
          "end": 169.86,
          "en": "and then scan this barcode here or the one in the terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "And then once you tap to open the link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 175.46,
          "en": "that is sent by that barcode, you should click Open,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.46,
          "end": 177.313,
          "en": "which opens the Expo Go app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.94,
          "end": 179.82999999999998,
          "en": "Then you should grant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.82999999999998,
          "end": 181.14,
          "en": "any permissions the app might (device chiming)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.14,
          "end": 182.183,
          "en": "be asking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.4,
          "end": 187.49,
          "en": "And now you see here that the JavaScript bundle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.49,
          "end": 188.42,
          "en": "is being built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.42,
          "end": 190.24,
          "en": "So the Expo app is being built.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.24,
          "end": 192.86,
          "en": "The React Native app based on Expo is built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.86,
          "end": 196.95,
          "en": "and it opens up in this simulator on our real device here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.95,
          "end": 199.1,
          "en": "So in this Expo Go app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 199.1,
          "end": 200.77,
          "en": "We can close this info screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 200.77,
          "end": 204.69,
          "en": "And now here, we see our app which we're building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.69,
          "end": 207.883,
          "en": "on our local machine running on a real device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.13,
          "end": 212.91,
          "en": "Now we can tell that this is our app by changing this text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.91,
          "end": 216.827,
          "en": "If I remove all the text here, and instead I say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 216.827,
          "end": 221.827,
          "en": "\"Hello, World,\" good old \"Hello, World\" message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.731,
          "end": 225.083,
          "en": "and I then save this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.73,
          "end": 229.32,
          "en": "you will see that it basically instantly updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.32,
          "end": 232.29,
          "en": "on your phone as well in this Expo Go app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.29,
          "end": 234.53,
          "en": "which we use for previewing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.53,
          "end": 237.9,
          "en": "And this is how simple it is to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.9,
          "end": 241.61,
          "en": "and test those Expo based React Native apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.61,
          "end": 244.75,
          "en": "with the Expo Go app and why it's so recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.75,
          "end": 246.87,
          "en": "to use this Expo workflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.87,
          "end": 248.03,
          "en": "It simply makes building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.03,
          "end": 251.51,
          "en": "and testing React Native apps much easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.51,
          "end": 254.75,
          "en": "And this still is a React Native app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.75,
          "end": 258.233,
          "en": "We're just using Expo to make our life a bit easier.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
